        "behaviour": [
          "Use the existing Screens shell and Choose/Design/Connect workflow. Keep the canvas beside one image inspector in wide windows.",
          "Use one clickable selected-asset row, a searchable typed UI-image chooser, and import staging/cancellation inside that chooser. Picker and canvas actions remain inert.",
          "Keep paired displayed dimensions, explicit aspect preservation, original-size restore and Apply/Cancel together. Disable unchanged Apply/Cancel; preserve numeric focus on Enter/Apply and Escape/Cancel.",
          "Retain drafts on invalid dimensions, missing/replaced/unreadable references, source conflict, selection changes, import cancellation and Source navigation. Put repair actions and field errors beside the relevant input.",
          "Review changed files explicitly. With aspect preservation on, retain width and derive the new displayed height from the replacement ratio; otherwise retain both dimensions.",
          "Add another ordinary image node in the same screen. Cancel returns to the previous selection; each image retains its draft. Preserve Source, shared Undo/Redo, reopen, order, confirmed removal and retained assets.",
          "Keep position/anchor units, alignment, size limits, parent constraints, ordering and removal under Layout. Preserve the earlier accepted composition, numeric and nested controls during production integration.",
          "Put editing first in compact windows, with Show preview and Edit image navigation. Keep the initial core controls and Apply visible at 560 by 640.",
          "Keep Source in the top toolbar and deliberate Test in Ren'Py beside the preview. Preserve dark, dense presentation, current fonts/icons and the absence of continuously repainting animation."
        ],
        "deviations": [
          "This approval covers browser presentation and sample interaction. Catalog/import, source writes, history, reopen, file replacement and previews use fictional browser-memory data; no native picker, project file, actual core decoder, SDK or game action runs.",
          "The HTML canvas and code-native artwork are schematic. Ren'Py geometry, inherited styling, source protection, persistence and real operation mappings require production qualification under #40.",
          "The full Design Lab gate has a retained startup-navigation failure. Focused rendering, interactions, source identity and approval/capture validation are tracked separately. This approval does not waive the combined-gate gap or product acceptance.",
          "Dynamic captures such as import, invalid-size and replacement review are reproduced by the interaction steps in refined-check.mjs rather than registered initial-state URLs."
        ]
      }
